{{!--
  Namespaced classic-Ember component invocation: `<Forms::TextInput>`.
  At runtime Ember's container resolver maps `Forms::TextInput` to
  `forms/text-input.hbs` — a slash-namespaced template path.

  Our by-name resolver in `lib/classic-resolver.ts` only handles
  single-segment kebab names (`<EsCard>` → `es-card.hbs`). It doesn't
  parse the `::` namespace separator and doesn't probe nested paths
  like `addon/components/forms/text-input.hbs`.

  Documents this limitation. The accompanying test is `it.fails(...)`
  so future namespaced-component support shows up as a passing test.
--}}
<form>
  <Forms::TextInput @value="hello" />
</form>
